News caching is merged into Quarry `main` (#14), and I've reviewed it. Each search's results are kept for 7 days. Results up to 30 days old are served when NewsFeed or the meta-search refuses, and an empty answer is remembered for 24 hours. A refusal is never mistaken for "no news". Quarry's local CI passed, along with 19 new tests.

**This needs your OK to reach production:** the caching ships in Quarry 0.3.17, release PR #13. Until that release is deployed, production behaves as before, and every news search still calls NewsFeed. Should I release and deploy 0.3.17?

